      "headline": "Mexico aviation authority faces FAA safety evaluation",
      "context": "The Mexican civil aviation authority will undergo US FAA assessment this week on safety standards compliance, with potential consequences for Mexico's aviation category ranking.",
      "background": "The FAA's International Aviation Safety Assessment program checks whether a country's civil aviation authority meets ICAO's minimum safety oversight standards. Mexico's AFAC has sought since 2023 to regain the FAA's top Category 1 safety ranking.",
      "view": "This week's review is only a snapshot, not a verdict. Rodríguez Garduño, a UNAM air law specialist, says a real outcome will take at least six months, so the immediate reporting cannot settle whether Mexico regains Category 1.",
      "prediction": "The FAA's conclusion, due within roughly six months per the specialist's estimate, will confirm whether AFAC's staffing, inspections and legislation meet ICAO standards or whether Mexico stays below Category 1.",
      "analysisV": 8,
